			<div class="content" id="post-content-4396172">
									

<p>So, I started writing this scip last May 14 this year, but didn't end up makng a drafts thread until just this late September cause I was busy at work and had a ton of personal issues.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▶&nbsp;See&nbsp;more&nbsp;author&nbsp;notes&nbsp;and&nbsp;possibly&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">◀&nbsp;Close&nbsp;author&nbsp;notes&nbsp;and&nbsp;possibly&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This was originally suppose to be a some sort of soul parasite of the &quot;Oversoul&quot;. The Oversoul is like humanity's collective souls and this thing is parasitizing it through humanity. It quickly became a complex idea since I also planning on adding a &quot;pop cap&quot; to humanity due to the Oversoul, where humans being born after 10 billion or 20 billion slowly become deforemd or even anomalous. Anyway, I wasn't really sure how to execute it so I scrapped it immediately.</p>
<p>Months pass, I was doing SEO, and finished my second game, I decided to give this SCP a second try.</p>
<p>This is when I added the &quot;pig&quot; part. It was originally a pig parasite so it just make sense that I add the pigs as a side effect. But then I started getting positive feedback on it. So I realized that yeah, &quot;<strong>something memetic obscuring humans and implanting the idea that they're pigs</strong>&quot; (as Mr. <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crayne" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1346995); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1346995&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1570900456" alt="Crayne" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1346995)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crayne" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1346995); return false;">Crayne</a></span> put it via PM) was a indeed pretty interesting. Although since this was not suppose to be the idea, I struggled to conceptualize further. I had to consult more people and get their feedback and see which works.</p>
<p>Now, either this SCP is about &quot;<strong>The Foundation thinks it's an anomaly that causes humans with knowledge of its properties to perceive certain pigs as having human qualities, while it is in fact an anomaly that causes certain humans to perceive affected humans as pigs</strong>&quot; as phrased by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/simartar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5489226); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5489226&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1570900456" alt="Simartar" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5489226)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/simartar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5489226); return false;">Simartar</a></span> or &quot;<strong>you saw and treated them as pigs while you didn't know about their anomalous nature. That their screams sound human if you know what they are, if you hear them talk when you know, but you just hear them squeal and oink when you don't</strong>&quot; as suggested by Mr. Crayne.</p>
<p>I pretty much hit bedrock in terms of conceptualizing about this scip so I decided to post it already.</p>
<p>I hope this didn't turn out to be something shit and wasted the effort of people that shaped it.</p>
<p>If you have any ideas or suggestions on how can I further improve this SCP, don't hesitate to comment it down. :)</p>
